#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186374577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cfa1f55-551a-5306-bd99-fea04c91ec1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{10}h+\\frac{7}{10}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374579} {:answer/id #uuid "3be49e71-5568-5d62-82d7-e93c7a49c9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}h+\\frac{1}{2}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374580} {:answer/id #uuid "34231eb7-95de-578d-b6fb-bea5404c4896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{2}{5}h+\\frac{3}{5}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374581} {:answer/id #uuid "9b15f0ef-62bd-5bf4-b839-6eaeb395f1ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{5}h+\\frac{2}{5}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374582} {:answer/id #uuid "90fd9287-b4a0-5691-951e-3bfea08cd342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90fd9287-b4a0-5691-951e-3bfea08cd342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374583} :answer-field/id #uuid "119c1703-b739-5d7d-ac80-fd52c955b62b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186374578}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94886abc-d5f4-549c-88a5-0c9095cd6221" :question/math-academy-id "q-120285" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-h+i \\\\  & =i-h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=3:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{3}{10}(i-h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =h+\\frac{3}{10}(i-h) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79faca23-cc2f-5c5c-b789-a9e286ea99d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388608} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0a43bc-5415-59c2-a9a7-0ed10cb2c862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79faca23-cc2f-5c5c-b789-a9e286ea99d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388608} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b100796-ab8c-5829-b7c0-21c5b307092c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b703e0c-1828-55e5-be16-9b8fa50851e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b703e0c-1828-55e5-be16-9b8fa50851e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388611} :answer-field/id #uuid "90b4534a-4d56-520e-9cbd-ca4ad433ac7c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388610}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9bf2d1d7-06cd-5a1b-a4ab-399010ca0c3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275128" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/992be4e67316804381ffc38860d2eaf23fd4a93cfe22ec4918c30c41e34ade57.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/c0f7f4df52373ca602aff41c97a5b8413f510353874540b76147c527a2f4b18c.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=\\frac{1}{2}|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-\\frac{1}{2}r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=\\frac{5}{2}|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-\\frac{5}{2}s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-\\frac{1}{2}r-\\frac{5}{2}s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{5}{2}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab12ad40-40b5-5bee-9964-a8d64a04e9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388614} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7d3a0c-e7f6-5a55-bf81-aa2123fac05b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{8}f+\\frac{1}{8}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388615} {:answer/id #uuid "bda315af-ccc9-53c8-9453-fbb1972c8fa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{8}{13}f+\\frac{5}{13}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388616} {:answer/id #uuid "c29743d4-d73f-5449-b4b1-5bffab50d228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{8}f+\\frac{1}{5}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388617} {:answer/id #uuid "76bea49f-dc71-5058-a5c5-11161bb656b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=f+\\frac{8}{5}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab12ad40-40b5-5bee-9964-a8d64a04e9d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388614} :answer-field/id #uuid "56048438-df7a-5832-ac34-4fcc26be6ddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cb79b649-cc96-59ab-927e-8bb7778fa82d" :question/math-academy-id "q-278290" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/36aeda6b6f5ce46552f55f458da60ef46a646d737c452d586389c03c47d1c9cb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ in the ratio $FP:PG=8:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{FP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OFG,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =\\overset{\\to }{FO}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-f+g \\\\  & =g-f.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $FP:PG=8:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{FP}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overset{\\to }{FG}=\\frac{8}{13}(g-f).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP} \\\\  & =f+\\frac{8}{13}(g-f) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388619 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector That Satisfies a Ratio in Terms of Known Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8af4c36e-bab6-59d8-baec-35aea10345a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8af4c36e-bab6-59d8-baec-35aea10345a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388621} :answer-field/id #uuid "6da47429-f7d2-5907-b203-fe3a3ba45214" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388620} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95cace35-39ca-5f5e-a7e0-d26cc53e39c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95cace35-39ca-5f5e-a7e0-d26cc53e39c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388623} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8304a8c-d3e7-59e7-aeca-7e8a7a4fbd1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388622}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6455512b-935f-5f04-b876-901ffd05fe90" :question/math-academy-id "q-322574" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/2a9cacfc6787e60229076c4abd2854709d51ac718c8d519256a61dbe92852b05.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{GH}$ in the ratio $GJ:JH=6:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}$ via the vectors $g$ and $h.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$g+$\n{{field-2}}\n$h$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{GJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OGH,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GH} & =\\overset{\\to }{GO}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{OH} \\\\  & =-g+h \\\\  & =h-g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $GJ:JH=6:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{GJ}=\\frac{6}{13}\\overset{\\to }{GH}=\\frac{6}{13}(h-g).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OG}+\\overset{\\to }{GJ} \\\\  & =g+\\frac{6}{13}(h-g) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}g+\\frac{6}{13}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Scalar Factors in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdd476cc-a4cb-5da9-b8ff-6933baa3d1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388626} {:answer/id #uuid "e5c8e722-de62-54b2-b677-05cd3fb0bdfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388627} {:answer/id #uuid "8394bc29-6eb8-5a02-98b9-82124768cb19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388628} {:answer/id #uuid "65bf3ec4-5baa-53f3-8995-f7e4ed5b61b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388629} {:answer/id #uuid "0224a99c-cfc4-5831-bca4-8024a57b6b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8394bc29-6eb8-5a02-98b9-82124768cb19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388628} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5ce4d46-4554-5581-b4ce-f52da3d43316" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d27e1410-6d2c-5849-b4f0-5d86e8924bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-42662" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/e2f149fb4f32fb264e0af6898e7737d570ec90bbff31cf1256eb9bd2636ceab3.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084598/assets/589f9f524a7c98da61ad6c5001b8d392d89073d5734cd70cfa750d153fe6f7b7.png)\n\nIn $△OUW$ shown above, we have \n\n- $OU=2|v|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OU}$ has the opposite direction to $v$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OU}=-2v.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $UW=4|u|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{UW}$ has the opposite direction to $u$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{UW}=-4u.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\overset{\\to }{OU}+\\overset{\\to }{UW} \\\\  & =-2v-4u \\\\  & =-4u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $w=\\lambda u+\\mu v=-4u-2v.$\n\nSince $u∦v,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-4$ and $\\mu =-2$"}]}
